rtl8370: add 802.1Q VLAN offload support

From upstream pull request 257 (turing-machines/BMC-Firmware), rebased
onto this fork's realtek-switch.patch. Three things had to be resolved,
and the last of them is why that pull request has never been merged.

One hunk rewrote a loop cosmetically and in doing so used upstream's
`priv->ds`, where this fork's driver has `&priv->ds`. The rewrite is
dropped and the fork's loop kept.

One hunk added the operations to a second `dsa_switch_ops` table.
Upstream has an smi/mdio pair; this driver has a single table. That hunk
is inapplicable and is dropped; the surviving one fills the table this
driver actually has.

AND THE PATCH IS MISSING A CLOSING BRACE. `rtl8365mb_port_vlan_add`
ends at its `return 0;` with no `}`, so `rtl8365mb_port_set_transparent`
and the two functions after it are parsed as nested definitions:
"invalid storage class for function". It cannot ever have been compiled.
The brace is added here.

Upstream: https://github.com/turing-machines/BMC-Firmware/pull/257
Signed-off-by: Oleg Tsarev <oleg@tsarev.id>

